WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
Hey, welcome to Tesla Short's Time, Episode 543.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.120
I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.180
Today is July 16th, 2026.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.180
Here's your Tesla news rundown.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.760
Tesla's Model Y, Robotaxi Fleet in Texas,

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:15.660
grew 50% in one day,

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.760
marking the first visible test

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.220
of scaled unsupervised operations.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.140
The National Transportation Safety Board

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.820
released its preliminary report

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.100
on the June crash in Katie, Texas.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.480
The report states the driver pressed the accelerator

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.280
to 100% and pushed speed above 70 miles per hour

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.860
on a 30 mile per hour residential road.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:41.300
The 2025 Model 3 operating under FSD

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.920
supervised continued straight

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.620
through a terminating intersection

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.400
and struck a residence.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.600
Findings align with Tesla's account

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.100
that manual override caused the incident.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.560
Electronic data from the vehicle

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.340
and security footage confirmed the driver input

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.680
under clear, dry, daylight conditions.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.280
The investigation remains ongoing

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:04.200
with no final probable cause determination yet.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:07.100
While regulators examined past incidents,

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.660
Tesla is already scaling its next generation operations

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.860
in the same state.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.820
Tesla added enough Model Y vehicles

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.320
to grow its Texas Robotaxi test fleet

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.140
by half within 24 hours.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.180
The expansion supports continued supervised FSD data collection

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.380
ahead of any unsupervised approval.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.760
Deployment remains tied to regulatory clearance

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.140
for broader operations.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.740
This is the first visible step in building fleet scale

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.700
for real world testing in Texas.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.300
The same Shanghai factory feeding Texas testing

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.780
is also driving Tesla's rising position in global trade.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:47.240
Tesla rose to sixth among Chinese exporters

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.660
after doubling overseas vehicle shipments

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:50.960
from its Shanghai plant.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.240
The ranking reflects higher output allocated

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.100
to international markets rather than domestic sales.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:00.640
Giga Shanghai remains the main source for European

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.520
and right-hand drive deliveries.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.980
The increase in export volume directly lifted

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:08.960
Tesla's position in the national exporter rankings.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.220
While Tesla's strengthens its export position,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.020
the company is also rethinking

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:15.860
fundamental vehicle architecture.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.340
Tesla, Ferrari, and BMW

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:20.880
are adopting lighter wiring alternatives

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.740
to replace copper harnesses.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.140
The change reduces vehicle weight and material costs

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.020
in next-generation platforms.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.860
Lower mass improves range and allows smaller batteries

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.180
for equivalent performance.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.380
The shift also reduces supply chain exposure

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.820
to copper price and availability constraints.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.620
The same drive toward lighter, more efficient platforms

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:45.280
is drawing new suppliers into Tesla's orbit.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.120
Xinjiang transmission filed for a Chi-next IPO

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.380
seeking $417 million.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:54.220
Proceeds are earmarked for components

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.740
supporting Tesla's Optimus Humanoid.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.400
Ballscrew revenue currently represents

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.680
less than 10% of the company's sales.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.580
The filing positions the firm for expected growth

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.780
in precision linear motion parts for humanoid robots.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.980
As Optimus attracts supplier investment,

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.760
Tesla faces renewed questions about its core vehicle business

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:15.760
in key markets.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.400
Germany's KBA registration data shows

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.840
Skoda surpassing Tesla in electric vehicle market share.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.780
Volkswagen's overall position weakened

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:29.200
even as total EV registrations rose in the country.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:32.220
Established volume brands captured share

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:34.140
amid broader competitive pressure.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.600
The shift highlights how traditional European makers

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.260
are gaining ground in the growing EV segment.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:44.140
European rivals are also challenging Tesla directly

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:45.340
in the sedan segment.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:50.780
The Mercedes-Benz CLA EV enters the compact luxury sedan segment

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.700
where the Model 3 has held strong sales positions.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:56.320
Comparison centers on differences in range,

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.580
charging speed, and interior features

00:03:58.580 --> 00:03:59.840
between the two vehicles.

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.920
Mercedes aims to contest Tesla's longstanding leadership

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:04.840
in this category.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:08.220
The new Model brings direct product competition

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:11.020
to a segment Tesla has dominated for years.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:13.420
While product rivals multiply,

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.920
Tesla continues expanding the infrastructure

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.360
that supports its vehicles.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.660
A new supercharger site is scheduled to open

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.800
on Isle of Palm's South Carolina.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:26.620
The station will operate under the open access policy

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.460
serving both Tesla and non-Tesla vehicles.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.700
The addition expands charging access along the coastal corridor.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.300
Local planning documents confirm the station will serve

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.640
both Tesla and non-Tesla vehicles

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.760
under the open access policy.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.680
The site adds to the growing network of open superchargers

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.600
available to drivers of multiple EV brands.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:52.640
Tesla responded to a strange supercharging pricing error

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.580
with refunds issued automatically.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:58.680
The glitch showed an inflated per minute rate in the app

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:02.000
at superchargers in Prince Edward Island and New Brunswick.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.840
The company processed full reimbursements

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.840
without requiring customer requests.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:10.220
Refunds covered the difference between the displayed

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.300
erroneous rate and the correct rate

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.820
for every affected session.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.360
The error was corrected after appearing in the app

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.360
before any further sessions occurred.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:22.600
Charging infrastructure supports not only cars

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.340
but also Tesla's commercial vehicle efforts.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:29.020
Paper transport added a Tesla semi to its fleet

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:32.280
as part of a multi-fuel strategy alongside diesel.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.280
Deployment focuses on routes with adequate

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:37.640
charging infrastructure for data collection.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.860
The carrier can now compare operating costs

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:44.200
and uptime across power trains on similar routes.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:48.120
The addition allows the carrier to gather real world data

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.120
on electric long haul economics.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.520
On a lighter note, Tesla's digital sales tools

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.360
continue to simplify ownership.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.900
Tesla posted that customers can complete an order

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.560
on the website in two minutes.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.240
They can finish the entire purchase inside the Tesla app.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.680
The update emphasizes a fully digital workflow

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.780
from selection to delivery without dealership visits.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:14.760
This continues Tesla's longstanding direct sales model.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:18.200
The process covers configuration, financing,

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.460
insurance and final paperwork all within the app

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.300
after the initial website order.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.500
Beyond day-to-day ownership,

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.960
Musk is preparing a longer-term showcase of Tesla's work.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:32.300
Elon Musk is constructing a product gallery

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.820
at his Texas Ranch to display historical

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:36.020
and current hardware.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:39.080
The facility will house inventions from Tesla,

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.220
SpaceX and related companies in one location.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.500
Plans include public or semi-public access

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.500
for viewing vehicles, rockets and other artifacts.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.960
The gallery will bring together vehicles, rockets

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:54.960
and other hardware developed across multiple companies

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:57.380
in a single visitor accessible space.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:01.880
Traders have cooled on prospects for a Tesla SpaceX merger.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.880
Polymarket probabilities for a Tesla SpaceX merger

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:07.560
have declined in recent trading.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:10.300
The drop reflects reduced enthusiasm

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.380
among prediction market participants ahead of earnings.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.880
No official statements from either company

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:17.660
have addressed merger speculation.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.640
The slide and odds occurred as traders adjusted positions

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.580
in the days leading into Tesla's quarterly results.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:29.980
Daily FSD users on X noted that the accelerator override

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:33.320
and speed profile in the Texas crash would be unusual

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:36.100
even on a vehicle's worst supervised day.

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:39.460
The observation reinforces Tesla's position

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:42.040
that the incident resulted from driver input

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:43.880
rather than autonomous control.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:47.160
Fleet data discussion shows how such events

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:50.200
can be distinguished from typical supervised behavior.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.160
Investors on trading platforms are pressing

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:56.540
for clearer timelines on both optimist production volumes

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:59.320
and unsupervised robo-taxi deployment.

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:04.020
The questions center on whether 2027 targets remain realistic,

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.100
given current factory and regulatory progress.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.260
Retail share holders are publicly questioning

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.740
earlier robo-taxi deployment promises

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:14.680
that have not yet materialized.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:18.080
The conversation centers on how updated timelines

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.560
might affect long-term valuation assumptions.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.180
There is a challenge worth discussing.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.860
An owner reported his one-year-old child

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:28.440
became trapped inside a charging cyber truck

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.700
as interior temperatures rose quickly.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.680
He stated he nearly had to break a window to reach the child.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.300
The incident points to a potential gap

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:40.280
in how door controls and climate systems behave

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:41.720
during charging sessions.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:44.880
Tesla has not yet issued a public response

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:47.940
or software adjustment tied to this specific case.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:51.160
The episode occurred while the owner stepped away

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:54.020
briefly to initiate charging, leaving the child

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:55.000
inside the vehicle.

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:58.300
The report underscores the importance of verifying

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.080
childlock and remote unlock functionality

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:04.160
in edge scenarios involving unattended charging.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.260
Vehicle wiring has historically been treated

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:10.160
as a fixed heavy subsystem whose mass penalty

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:12.860
is accepted in exchange for reliable power

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.140
and signal distribution.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:17.760
Tesla's move alongside Ferrari and BMW

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:20.960
to replace copper harnesses with lighter substitutes

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:23.500
attacks that assumption at the material level.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:26.400
The change directly reduces curb weight

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.620
which improves both range and the cost

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:31.540
of every other component sized to carry that mass.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:35.660
Lower copper content also alters supply chain exposure

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:38.280
by shrinking reliance on a constrained metal.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:41.240
The savings appear in bill of materials cost

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:44.120
yet they compound across every vehicle produced

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:46.200
once the new architecture is in place.

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:49.540
The practical test will be whether the lighter harness

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.980
maintains signal integrity and durability

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:55.180
across temperature cycles and vibration profiles.

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:58.420
If the substitution holds the industry gains

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.700
a structural cost and efficiency lever

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:04.020
that does not depend on battery chemistry breakthroughs.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:07.080
Keep an eye on any updates from the NTSB

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.600
as the Katie investigation moves forward.

